  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1124 PM CST Tue Nov 3 2026\n\nActive weather continues... Drier air brought a few longer breaks\nto the on and off showers early overnight but the next round of \nmoisture will be set to arrive early Wednesday, bringing back \nbetter shower coverage for the morning hours. Southerly flow then \ncontinues at the surface during the day, but winds aloft are \nexpected to shift westwards, which will push out the better \nmoisture and possibly bring a longer break in the active weather \nfor the afternoon and evening hours, especially in east-central \nWisconsin. Some light showers are still expected to return by \nWednesday night into Thursday however, as wrap around moisture and\nlingering upper support around the active low provide enough \nforcing. No thunderstorms are expected in the forecast at this \ntime, so all mentions of storms have been removed. Additional \nprecipitation totals will mainly be focused across northern \nWisconsin with around 60-80% chance of at least an additional half\nan inch of rainfall north of a line of Merrill to Wausaukee. \nThese same areas also have around 20-30% chance for an additional \ninch of rainfall starting tomorrow morning. Further south, where \nthe moisture departs this afternoon, the probability of exceeding \nhalf an inch of additional rainfall now sits around 20 or less for\nthe Fox Valley. \n\nBehind the departing system, blustery northwest winds can be\nexpected that will usher in cooler air Thursday night. Above\nnormal temperatures are expected for most of the forecast, the\nonly exception being Friday which may be closer to normal. Mainly\ndry conditions expected Friday through Tuesday.",
